#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""THE CONTROLLER'S APPLY SCRIPT: the root half of Mercury's controller app deploy channel (the SDN
platform design revision 6, section 10 H, change C and C2; P6).

Installed ROOT-OWNED as /usr/local/sbin/mercury-ryu-apply on the controller host by
scripts/host-steps/p6-controller-apply-install.sh, which fixes the constants below when it
renders the copy it installs. It is never run from the repository, and the one sudoers line
(`mercury ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/mercury-ryu-apply ""`) lets the deploy account
run it with NO arguments and nothing else.

It treats what the deploy account wrote as a REQUEST, never an instruction. A request is one of
TWO KINDS, told apart by its shape and nothing else:
- the APPLY (a set of apps): exactly {"apps": [...], "listen": {"host", "port"}}, with no
  "kind" key, the shape every request had before the second kind, so a recorded request keeps
  its hash (`request_sha256`) and its drop-in render byte for byte;
- the PUT-BACK (decision K3, the operator's of 2026-11-07: a first deploy's rollback): exactly
  {"kind": "put-before-back", "before_sha256": <64 hex>}, steps P1 to P3 below.
A request naming any other kind, or a kind with any other key, is refused by name.

The apply, step by step:
- C2, before the request is read: while the controller's unit runs as root (its User empty or
  root) and the app folder is writable by the deploy account, the deploy account could plant
  code root runs at the next restart, so nothing is done; the refusal names the unit's User and
  the folder's owner and mode;
- 1. the one staging file, APPS_ROOT/.apply/request.json, is opened without following a link and
  must be a regular file owned by the deploy account, with one link, at most MAX_BYTES, and
  exactly the shape {"apps": [{"name", "version", "sha256"[, "config_sha256"]}, ...], "listen":
  {"host", "port"}}, the apps in load order; anything else is refused by name, never quoting its
  content;
- 2. every name matches NAME and every version VERSION;
- 3. every APPS_ROOT/<name>/<version>/ is a real directory under APPS_ROOT (its realpath is
  itself), owned by the deploy account, holding <name>.py, nothing in it a link, writable by
  group or others, or owned by anyone else, and its recomputed content hash (`folder_hash`, the
  same framing as Mercury's `modules/jobs/lifecycle.content_hash`, from the files' bytes) equal
  to the request's, so a folder edited after staging is refused;
- 3b. an app's start-time config (decision K9; C2707) is the file beside its version,
  APPS_ROOT/<name>/<version>.config.json (`config_path`), outside the version's folder so the
  Published folder's hash stays the reviewed code's. With config_sha256 in the request it must
  be a regular file of the deploy account's, one link, not writable by group or others, at most
  MAX_BYTES, a JSON object in UTF-8, and its sha256 the request's; without it, no such file may
  be there (the app would read a config nobody confirmed). The script never reads a value from
  it and never needs a secret: Mercury refuses a config holding one before it is staged;
- 3c. the app SDK (C2852, option A): a request may name it, ``"sdk": {"sha256"}`` beside apps
  and listen (a request without it keeps its hash and its render); its folder,
  APPS_ROOT/.sdk/<sha256>/ (`sdk_folder`), is held to step 3's rules and must hold
  mercury_app/__init__.py, its recomputed content hash the request's (`check_sdk`). The drop-in
  then carries ``Environment=PYTHONPATH=`` that folder, so every app imports the confirmed SDK;
  an app named mercury_app is refused (it would shadow it);
- 4. listen.host parses as an IPv4 or IPv6 address and listen.port is in 1024 to 65535;
- 4b. THE UNIT'S OWN ARGUMENTS ARE CARRIED (C2675, C2985): the command line the unit runs
  without Mercury's drop-in (`unit_command`: the ExecStart `systemctl cat` shows in the unit
  file and every drop-in read before mercury.conf) is read by this script, as root, and what of
  it is not Mercury's to manage is kept (`keep_from`): Ryu's REST bind (`--wsapi-host`,
  `--wsapi-port`), every other flag, and every app the unit loads that Mercury does not manage
  (a file by its absolute path, or a module). A request names what it carries as ``"keep"``
  beside apps and listen (a request without it keeps its hash and its render), and the script
  COMPARES that with what it read: a difference is refused naming both, so the kept arguments
  are never taken from the request, only confirmed by it. An argument that is not one plain
  word (quoted, escaped, or expanded by systemd) is refused by its position, a drop-in read
  after mercury.conf that sets ExecStart is refused by name (Mercury's would not be the command
  line that runs), and a kept app's file that is not there is refused before anything is
  written. A kept file an app of the request replaces (the same name) is left out, by rule;
- 5. it renders the ONE drop-in, DROPIN_ROOT/<unit>.d/mercury.conf: `User=` RYU_USER, an empty
  `ExecStart=`, then RYU_MANAGER with the fixed flags, the listen address, the kept REST bind
  and flags, the kept apps, the request's apps' files in order, then BUILTIN_APPS
  (`render_dropin`; Mercury previews the same text). REST's bind is the unit's own or none:
  the script never writes one the unit did not have, so it cannot widen it;
- 6. writes it atomically, keeping the previous one as mercury.conf.prev;
- 7. runs `systemctl daemon-reload`, then restarts the unit;
- 8. judges success by IDENTITY: the unit's MainPID changed, it is active, and its User is
  RYU_USER, within UP_BOUND_S, counted on this script's MONOTONIC clock (C2983: the
  controller's wall clock steps when NTP corrects it after a boot, C2982, and a bound on it
  would read years elapsed);
- 9. writes the outcome to OUTCOME_DIR/outcome.json (0644) and appends it to history.jsonl. Its
  ``started`` and ``finished`` are the controller's wall clock, a record and never a bound.

The put-back puts the drop-in before Mercury's last apply back, which that apply kept as
mercury.conf.prev (step 6). It does NOT remove mercury.conf: on S3's layout the drop-in before
the first deploy is mercury.conf itself (deploy/controller/mercury.conf, `User=ryu` only), so
removing it would leave the unit on its own User, root, which is C2's unsafe state and which the
identity check would refuse every time.
- P1. mercury.conf.prev must be a regular file (no link) owned by the account this script runs
  as, not writable by group or others, at most MAX_BYTES, and its hash (`before_sha256`: of its
  text with leading and trailing blank lines dropped, as `systemctl cat` shows it and Mercury's
  plan read it) the request's before_sha256, so what is put back is what the plan showed;
- P2. its last `User=` line must be `User=` RYU_USER, so the put-back never runs Ryu as root;
- P3. it is written as mercury.conf atomically (mercury.conf.prev is kept as it is, so a second
  put-back puts the same drop-in back), then steps 7 to 9 as for an apply.

**What landed, in the outcome.** A refusal (`refused`) and an outcome with neither `refused`
nor `step` (an exception before mercury.conf was replaced) changed no drop-in; an outcome with a
`step` (daemon-reload, restart, wait, after-write or running) wrote the new drop-in, and every
failure past that write carries its step, so Mercury's rollback undoes what landed.

It never runs anything from APPS_ROOT as root, never takes a path or a command from the request
(a kept argument is the unit's own, read by this script and only compared with the request's),
and never rolls back by itself: a rollback is Mercury's second request (the previous set, or the
put-back), and mercury.conf.prev is also the break-glass. Written for the controller's Python
3.5 (Ubuntu 16.04.5): no f-strings, no variable annotations, nothing newer than 3.5
(tests/test_controller_apply.py checks it with Mercury's Python 3.5 check).

**The host step's read (`unit_read`).** scripts/host-steps/p6-controller-apply-install.sh loads
this file from the release, as the operator and never through sudo's one line, and calls
`unit_read(<unit>)`: the same `unit_command` and `keep_from`, so what the install accepts is
what a deploy carries. It prints the unit's ryu-manager, where Ryu's REST answers on the host
itself, and each kept app's file, or the refusal, and changes nothing.
"""

import errno
import fcntl
import grp
import hashlib
import ipaddress
import json
import os
import pwd
import re
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import time

# -- Fixed when installed (scripts/host-steps/p6-controller-apply-install.sh renders the
# -- placeholders; a copy with one left unrendered refuses to run). Never read from the request.
RYU_UNIT = "@RYU_UNIT@"
RYU_MANAGER = "@RYU_MANAGER@"
RYU_USER = "ryu"
DEPLOY_USER = "mercury"
APPS_ROOT = "/opt/ryu-apps"
DROPIN_ROOT = "/etc/systemd/system"
OUTCOME_DIR = "/var/lib/mercury-ryu-apply"
SYSTEMCTL = "/bin/systemctl"
REQUIRE_ROOT = True
# -- End of the installed constants.

#: The flags every rendered command line carries: links are what Mercury's post-check reads
#: (`/v1.0/topology/links` needs --observe-links; modules/sdn/drivers/ryu.py NO_TOPOLOGY_APP).
FIXED_FLAGS = ("--observe-links",)
#: Ryu's own apps, loaded after the managed ones: Mercury's reads (`/stats/...`,
#: `/v1.0/topology/...`) are theirs.
BUILTIN_APPS = ("ryu.app.ofctl_rest", "ryu.app.rest_topology")
#: How long the restarted unit has to be active with a new MainPID: 75 s, 2.5 times 30 s.
#: MEASURED at the controller's reboot test of 2026-11-11: Ryu answered within 30 s of its
#: process starting, and the unit is active sooner than Ryu answers, so 30 s is the outer
#: figure. Counted on the monotonic clock (C2983), and named in every outcome it fires in.
UP_BOUND_S = 75
UP_BOUND_SOURCE = ("2.5 times the 30 s within which Ryu answered after its process started, "
                   "measured at the controller's reboot test of 2026-11-11; counted on this "
                   "script's monotonic clock, never the controller's wall clock")
POLL_S = 1.0
#: One argument of the unit's own command line that is carried: a plain word (no space, quote,
#: backslash, `$` or `%`, which systemd would unquote or expand), so a carried argument is one
#: word of the rendered ExecStart exactly as the unit holds it.
TOKEN = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_@+=:,./-]{1,255}$")
#: An app the unit loads that Mercury does not manage: a file by its absolute path, or a
#: module by its dotted name (ryu-manager takes either).
APP_FILE = re.compile(r"^/[A-Za-z0-9_@+=:,./-]{0,250}[A-Za-z0-9_]\.py$")
APP_MODULE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)*$")
EXEC_LINE = re.compile(r"^\s*ExecStart\s*=(.*)$")
UNIT_NAME = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.@-]{0,63}\.service$")
#: Ryu's REST bind, the unit's own (C2675): carried as the unit has it, never written when the
#: unit names none.
REST_FLAGS = {"--wsapi-host": "host", "--wsapi-port": "port"}
#: The OpenFlow listen flags are the request's (``listen``: NetBox's openflow Service).
LISTEN_FLAGS = {"--ofp-listen-host": "host", "--ofp-tcp-listen-port": "port"}
#: A bind to every address of the host, in either family.
WILDCARDS = ("0.0.0.0", "::")
#: Where Ryu's REST answers when the unit names no port, and on the host itself when it names
#: no address (`unit_read`, for the host step's own check).
REST_DEFAULT_PORT = 8080
LOOPBACK = {4: "127.0.0.1", 6: "::1"}
MAX_KEEP = 64
MAX_BYTES = 64 * 1024
MAX_APPS = 32
NAME = re.compile(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,40}$")
VERSION = re.compile(r"^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$")
SHA256 = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$")
#: The framing Mercury's content hash starts with (modules/jobs/lifecycle.HASH_FRAMING).
HASH_FRAMING = b"mercury-git-folder-sha256-v2\0"
REQUEST_REL = os.path.join(".apply", "request.json")
DROPIN_NAME = "mercury.conf"
PREV_SUFFIX = ".prev"
#: The second request kind (decision K3): put the drop-in before Mercury's last apply back.
PUT_BACK = "put-before-back"
#: An app's start-time config sits beside its version's folder (decision K9; `config_path`).
CONFIG_SUFFIX = ".config.json"
#: The app SDK's folders (C2852, option A): APPS_ROOT/.sdk/<its content hash>/, each holding
#: the package mercury_app (`SDK_ENTRY`), put on the apps' import path by the drop-in's
#: PYTHONPATH. Content-addressed, so a version staged once is never written over by another
#: and a rollback to an earlier request finds its SDK where it left it.
SDK_DIR = ".sdk"
SDK_PACKAGE = "mercury_app"
SDK_ENTRY = os.path.join(SDK_PACKAGE, "__init__.py")
ENV ={"PATH": "/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin", "LANG": "C", "LC_ALL": "C"}


class Refused(Exception):
    """Refused before anything changed; the message is the whole reason."""


def iso(epoch=None):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(time.time() if epoch is None
                                                           else epoch))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the host runs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def systemctl(*args):
    proc = subprocess.run((SYSTEMCTL,) + tuple(args), stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                          stderr=subprocess.PIPE, universal_newlines=True, env=ENV,
                          timeout=120)
    return proc.returncode, proc.stdout, proc.stderr


def unit_properties(*names):
    """The unit's properties as systemd answers `show -p` (systemd 229 has no --value)."""
    args = ["show"]
    for n in names:
        args += ["-p", n]
    rc, out, err = systemctl(*(args + [RYU_UNIT]))
    if rc != 0:
        raise Refused("systemctl show {} answered {} ({}): its User cannot be read, so "
                      "nothing was done".format(RYU_UNIT, rc, (err or "").strip()[:120]))
    props = {}
    for line in out.splitlines():
        key, sep, value = line.partition("=")
        if sep:
            props[key.strip()] = value.strip()
    return props


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C2: the unsafe state, checked before the request is read
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def mode_words(st):
    return stat.filemode(st.st_mode)


def owner_words(st):
    try:
        user = pwd.getpwuid(st.st_uid).pw_name
    except KeyError:
        user = str(st.st_uid)
    try:
        group = grp.getgrgid(st.st_gid).gr_name
    except KeyError:
        group = str(st.st_gid)
    return "{}:{}".format(user, group)


def writable_by(st, account):
    """Whether *account* can write a directory of stat *st*: its owner with the owner's write
    bit, a member of its group with the group's, or anyone with the others' bit."""
    if st.st_mode & stat.S_IWOTH:
        return True
    if st.st_uid == account.pw_uid and st.st_mode & stat.S_IWUSR:
        return True
    if st.st_mode & stat.S_IWGRP:
        try:
            members = grp.getgrgid(st.st_gid).gr_mem
        except KeyError:
            members = []
        if st.st_gid == account.pw_gid or account.pw_name in members:
            return True
    return False


def unsafe_refusal(user, st, account):
    """"" or why: the unit's *user* is root (or empty) and APPS_ROOT, of stat *st*, is
    writable by the deploy *account*."""
    if user not in ("", "root"):
        return ""
    if not writable_by(st, account):
        return ""
    return ("refused before the request was read: {}'s User is {} (root) and {} is {} {}, "
            "writable by {}; code {} can write would run as root at the next restart. "
            "Move the unit to User={} first (S3 step 1), then change the folder's owner".format(
                RYU_UNIT, repr(user or ""), APPS_ROOT, owner_words(st), mode_words(st),
                DEPLOY_USER, DEPLOY_USER, RYU_USER))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1 to 4: the request
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _no_duplicates(pairs):
    out = {}
    for key, value in pairs:
        if key in out:
            raise Refused("the request names the key {} twice".format(json.dumps(key)[:60]))
        out[key] = value
    return out


def read_request(account):
    """The request's bytes, opened without following a link (step 1's file checks), and
    removed once read, so a request is applied once."""
    folder = os.path.join(APPS_ROOT, ".apply")
    try:
        dfd = os.open(folder, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    except OSError as exc:
        if exc.errno == errno.ENOENT:
            raise Refused("no request: {} does not exist".format(folder))
        raise Refused("{} could not be opened as a directory without following a link ({})"
                      .format(folder, exc.strerror))
    try:
        dst = os.fstat(dfd)
        if dst.st_uid != account.pw_uid:
            raise Refused("{} is owned by {}, not {}".format(folder, owner_words(dst),
                                                             DEPLOY_USER))
        try:
            fd = os.open("request.json", os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK,
                         dir_fd=dfd)
        except OSError as exc:
            if exc.errno == errno.ENOENT:
                raise Refused("no request: {} does not exist".format(
                    os.path.join(APPS_ROOT, REQUEST_REL)))
            if exc.errno == errno.ELOOP:
                raise Refused("the request {} is a symbolic link, not a regular file".format(
                    os.path.join(APPS_ROOT, REQUEST_REL)))
            raise Refused("the request could not be opened ({})".format(exc.strerror))
        try:
            st = os.fstat(fd)
            where = os.path.join(APPS_ROOT, REQUEST_REL)
            if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
                raise Refused("the request {} is not a regular file".format(where))
            if st.st_uid != account.pw_uid:
                raise Refused("the request {} is owned by {}, not {}".format(
                    where, owner_words(st), DEPLOY_USER))
            if st.st_nlink != 1:
                raise Refused("the request {} has {} links, not 1".format(where, st.st_nlink))
            if st.st_size > MAX_BYTES:
                raise Refused("the request {} is {} bytes, more than {}".format(
                    where, st.st_size, MAX_BYTES))
            raw = os.read(fd, MAX_BYTES + 1)
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
        try:
            os.unlink("request.json", dir_fd=dfd)
        except OSError:
            pass
    finally:
        os.close(dfd)
    if len(raw) > MAX_BYTES:
        raise Refused("the request is more than {} bytes".format(MAX_BYTES))
    return raw


def parse_put_back(doc):
    """The put-back's exact shape (decision K3): {"kind": PUT_BACK, "before_sha256": hex}."""
    kind = doc["kind"]
    if kind != PUT_BACK:
        raise Refused("the request's kind is not {} (the one kind a request names; an apply "
                      "names none)".format(PUT_BACK))
    if sorted(doc) != ["before_sha256", "kind"]:
        raise Refused("a {} request is not an object of exactly the keys kind and "
                      "before_sha256".format(PUT_BACK))
    value = doc["before_sha256"]
    if not isinstance(value, str) or not SHA256.match(value):
        raise Refused("before_sha256 does not match {}".format(SHA256.pattern))
    return {"kind": PUT_BACK, "before_sha256": value}


def parse_request(raw):
    """Steps 1, 2 and 4: the request's exact shape, each field named, never its value. A
    request with a "kind" key is the put-back (`parse_put_back`); one without is an apply."""
    try:
        doc = json.loads(raw.decode("utf-8"), object_pairs_hook=_no_duplicates)
    except (UnicodeDecodeError, ValueError):
        raise Refused("the request is not JSON in UTF-8")
    if isinstance(doc, dict) and "kind" in doc:
        return parse_put_back(doc)
    if not isinstance(doc, dict) or set(("apps", "listen")) - set(doc) \
            or set(doc) - set(("apps", "listen", "sdk", "keep")):
        raise Refused("the request is not an object of exactly the keys apps and listen (and "
                      "sdk, for a set given the app SDK, and keep, for a unit whose own "
                      "arguments are carried)")
    keep = check_keep(doc["keep"]) if "keep" in doc else None
    sdk = None
    if "sdk" in doc:
        sdk = doc["sdk"]
        if not isinstance(sdk, dict) or sorted(sdk) != ["sha256"]:
            raise Refused("sdk is not an object of exactly sha256")
        if not isinstance(sdk["sha256"], str) or not SHA256.match(sdk["sha256"]):
            raise Refused("sdk.sha256 does not match {}".format(SHA256.pattern))
    apps = doc["apps"]
    if not isinstance(apps, list) or len(apps) > MAX_APPS:
        raise Refused("apps is not a list of at most {} apps".format(MAX_APPS))
    seen = set()
    for i, app in enumerate(apps):
        where = "apps[{}]".format(i)
        if not isinstance(app, dict) or sorted(app) not in (
                ["name", "sha256", "version"], ["config_sha256", "name", "sha256", "version"]):
            raise Refused("{} is not an object of exactly name, version and sha256 (and "
                          "config_sha256, for an app with a config)".format(where))
        for key, rule in (("name", NAME), ("version", VERSION), ("sha256", SHA256),
                          ("config_sha256", SHA256)):
            if key not in app:
                continue
            value = app[key]
            if not isinstance(value, str) or not rule.match(value):
                raise Refused("{}.{} does not match {}".format(where, key, rule.pattern))
        if app["name"] in seen:
            raise Refused("{}.name names an app listed before it".format(where))
        if app["name"] == SDK_PACKAGE:
            raise Refused("{}.name is {}, the app SDK's package: an app of that name would "
                          "shadow the SDK every app imports".format(where, SDK_PACKAGE))
        seen.add(app["name"])
    listen = doc["listen"]
    if not isinstance(listen, dict) or sorted(listen) != ["host", "port"]:
        raise Refused("listen is not an object of exactly host and port")
    host, port = listen["host"], listen["port"]
    if not isinstance(host, str):
        raise Refused("listen.host is not a string")
    try:
        host = str(ipaddress.ip_address(host))
    except ValueError:
        raise Refused("listen.host does not parse as an IPv4 or IPv6 address")
    if isinstance(port, bool) or not isinstance(port, int) or not 1024 <= port <= 65535:
        raise Refused("listen.port is not a whole number from 1024 to 65535")
    out = {"apps": [dict(a) for a in apps], "listen": {"host": host, "port": port}}
    if sdk is not None:
        out["sdk"] = {"sha256": sdk["sha256"]}
    if keep is not None:
        out["keep"] = keep
    return out


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4b: the unit's own command line, and what of it is carried (C2675, C2985)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def unit_command(cat_text, unit):
    """The command line *unit* runs without Mercury's drop-in, from `systemctl cat <unit>`'s
    answer *cat_text*: ``{"argv": [words] or None, "file", "later": [files]}``. *argv* is the
    one ExecStart left by the unit file and every drop-in read BEFORE mercury.conf (an empty
    ``ExecStart=`` resets, as systemd reads it; a trailing backslash continues the line), None
    when the answer holds none; *file* is the file that set it; *later* names each file read
    AFTER mercury.conf that sets ExecStart, which would run in place of Mercury's. Refuses more
    than one ExecStart, an argument that is not one plain word (`TOKEN`) by its position,
    never its text, and a command that does not start with an absolute path."""
    mine = "# {}/{}.d/{}".format(DROPIN_ROOT, unit, DROPIN_NAME)
    lines = str(cat_text or "").splitlines()
    found, later, current, in_mine, past_mine, i = [], [], "", False, False, 0
    while i < len(lines):
        line = lines[i]
        i += 1
        if line.startswith("# /"):
            past_mine = past_mine or in_mine
            in_mine = line.strip() == mine
            current = line[2:].strip()
            continue
        m = EXEC_LINE.match(line)
        if not m:
            continue
        value = m.group(1).strip()
        while value.endswith("\\") and i < len(lines):
            value = (value[:-1] + " " + lines[i]).strip()
            i += 1
        if in_mine:
            continue
        if past_mine:
            if current not in later:
                later.append(current)
        elif not value:
            found = []
        else:
            found.append((value, current))
    if not found:
        return {"argv": None, "file": "", "later": later}
    if len(found) > 1:
        raise Refused("{} sets ExecStart {} times outside {} ({}): which command line it runs "
                      "cannot be told".format(unit, len(found), DROPIN_NAME, ", ".join(
                          sorted(set(f or "its unit file" for _, f in found)))))
    value, where = found[0]
    argv = value.split()
    for n, word in enumerate(argv):
        if not TOKEN.match(word):
            raise Refused("argument {} of {}'s ExecStart ({}) is not one plain word (letters, "
                          "digits and _ @ + = : , . / -): a quoted, escaped or expanded "
                          "argument cannot be carried as it is".format(
                              n, unit, where or "its unit file"))
    if not argv[0].startswith("/"):
        raise Refused("{}'s ExecStart ({}) does not start with a program's absolute path"
                      .format(unit, where or "its unit file"))
    return {"argv": argv, "file": where, "later": later}


def _is_app(word):
    """Whether *word* reads as an app wherever it stands: a file ending .py, or a dotted
    module name. (A bare word after a flag is that flag's value.)"""
    return word.endswith(".py") or ("." in word and bool(APP_MODULE.match(word)))


def keep_from(argv):
    """``(keep, listen)`` for the unit's own command line *argv* (`unit_command`'s): *keep* is
    what a deploy carries, in the request's shape (`check_keep`), or None when the unit has
    nothing but Mercury's own; *listen* is the OpenFlow listen the unit names (``{"host",
    "port"}``, each only when given), which is the request's to set. Carried: Ryu's REST bind
    (`REST_FLAGS`), every other flag with the word after it when that word is neither a flag
    nor an app, and every app but Ryu's built-ins (which every render loads). The fixed flags
    are every render's. Refuses, by position, a flag given twice or with no value and a word
    that is none of these."""
    rest, listen, flags, apps, i = {}, {}, [], [], 1
    while i < len(argv):
        at, word = i, argv[i]
        i += 1
        name, eq, value = word.partition("=")
        if name in REST_FLAGS or name in LISTEN_FLAGS:
            if not eq:
                if i >= len(argv):
                    raise Refused("{} is the unit's last argument and has no value".format(name))
                value = argv[i]
                i += 1
            into = rest if name in REST_FLAGS else listen
            key = REST_FLAGS.get(name) or LISTEN_FLAGS[name]
            if key in into:
                raise Refused("{} is given twice in the unit's command line".format(name))
            into[key] = value
        elif word in FIXED_FLAGS or word in BUILTIN_APPS:
            continue
        elif word.startswith("-"):
            flags.append(word)
            if not eq and i < len(argv) and not argv[i].startswith("-") \
                    and not _is_app(argv[i]):
                flags.append(argv[i])
                i += 1
        elif word.endswith(".py") or APP_MODULE.match(word):
            if word in apps:
                raise Refused("argument {} of the unit's command line loads an app it "
                              "already loads".format(at))
            apps.append(word)
        else:
            raise Refused("argument {} of the unit's command line is neither a flag, an app's "
                          "file ending .py nor a module's name".format(at))
    keep = {}
    if rest:
        if "port" in rest:
            if not rest["port"].isdigit():
                raise Refused("the unit's --wsapi-port is not a whole number")
            rest["port"] = int(rest["port"])
        keep["rest"] = rest
    if flags:
        keep["flags"] = flags
    if apps:
        keep["apps"] = apps
    return (check_keep(keep) if keep else None), listen


def check_keep(keep):
    """The request's ``keep`` in its exact shape, each field named, never its value:
    ``{"rest": {"host", "port"}, "flags": [words], "apps": [files and modules]}``, each key
    only when the unit has it. REST's host is one plain word that parses as an IPv4 or IPv6
    address (a name is not carried: refusing by resemblance is safe), kept as the unit writes
    it; its port a whole number from 1 to 65535; a flag one plain word; an app a file by its
    absolute path ending .py or a module's name, never one of Ryu's built-ins and never
    twice."""
    if not isinstance(keep, dict) or not keep or set(keep) - set(("rest", "flags", "apps")):
        raise Refused("keep is not an object of rest, flags and apps (each only when the unit "
                      "has it)")
    out = {}
    if "rest" in keep:
        rest = keep["rest"]
        if not isinstance(rest, dict) or not rest or set(rest) - set(("host", "port")):
            raise Refused("keep.rest is not an object of host and port (each only when the "
                          "unit names it)")
        got = {}
        if "host" in rest:
            host = rest["host"]
            if not isinstance(host, str) or not TOKEN.match(host):
                raise Refused("keep.rest.host is not one plain word")
            try:
                ipaddress.ip_address(host)
            except ValueError:
                raise Refused("keep.rest.host (the unit's --wsapi-host) does not parse as an "
                              "IPv4 or IPv6 address; a name is not carried")
            got["host"] = host
        if "port" in rest:
            port = rest["port"]
            if isinstance(port, bool) or not isinstance(port, int) or not 1 <= port <= 65535:
                raise Refused("keep.rest.port (the unit's --wsapi-port) is not a whole number "
                              "from 1 to 65535")
            got["port"] = port
        out["rest"] = got
    for key in ("flags", "apps"):
        if key not in keep:
            continue
        words = keep[key]
        if not isinstance(words, list) or not words or len(words) > MAX_KEEP:
            raise Refused("keep.{} is not a list of 1 to {} words".format(key, MAX_KEEP))
        for n, word in enumerate(words):
            where = "keep.{}[{}]".format(key, n)
            if not isinstance(word, str) or not TOKEN.match(word):
                raise Refused("{} is not one plain word".format(where))
            if key == "apps":
                if not (APP_FILE.match(word) if word.endswith(".py")
                        else APP_MODULE.match(word)):
                    raise Refused("{} is neither a file by its absolute path ending .py nor a "
                                  "module's name".format(where))
                if word in BUILTIN_APPS:
                    raise Refused("{} is one of Ryu's own apps every drop-in loads, never a "
                                  "kept one".format(where))
                if word in words[:n]:
                    raise Refused("{} names an app listed before it".format(where))
        out[key] = list(words)
    return out


def superseded(app, names):
    """Whether the kept *app* is a file an app of the request replaces: one of *names* is its
    file's name without .py. (Two apps of one name cannot load in one ryu-manager.)"""
    return app.endswith(".py") and os.path.basename(app)[:-3] in names


def kept_apps(request):
    """The kept apps the drop-in loads: the request's ``keep.apps`` in the unit's order,
    without each file an app of the request replaces (`superseded`)."""
    names = set(a["name"] for a in request["apps"])
    return [a for a in (request.get("keep") or {}).get("apps") or []
            if not superseded(a, names)]


def rest_url(rest):
    """Where Ryu's REST answers ON THE HOST ITSELF for the kept bind *rest* (``{"host",
    "port"}``, each only when the unit names it): the address it is bound to, loopback of the
    same family when it is bound to every address, IPv4 loopback when the unit names none
    (Ryu's default binds every IPv4 address); an IPv6 address bracketed, as a URL must."""
    host = rest.get("host")
    if host is None:
        host = LOOPBACK[4]
    else:
        ip = ipaddress.ip_address(host)
        if ip.is_unspecified:
            host = LOOPBACK[ip.version]
        if ip.version == 6:
            host = "[{}]".format(host)
    return "http://{}:{}".format(host, rest.get("port", REST_DEFAULT_PORT))


def read_unit(unit):
    """``(argv, keep, listen)`` for *unit* as systemd holds it now (`systemctl cat`), each
    refusal naming what was read: no answer, a drop-in read after Mercury's that sets
    ExecStart, or no ExecStart at all."""
    rc, out, err = systemctl("cat", unit)
    if rc != 0:
        raise Refused("systemctl cat {} answered {} ({}): the unit's own command line cannot "
                      "be read, so nothing was done".format(unit, rc, (err or "").strip()[:120]))
    got = unit_command(out, unit)
    if got["later"]:
        raise Refused("{} sets ExecStart and is read after {}: Mercury's drop-in would not be "
                      "the command line {} runs, so nothing was done".format(
                          ", ".join(got["later"]), DROPIN_NAME, unit))
    if got["argv"] is None:
        raise Refused("systemctl cat {} shows no ExecStart outside {}: what the unit runs "
                      "without Mercury's drop-in cannot be told, so nothing was done".format(
                          unit, DROPIN_NAME))
    keep, listen = keep_from(got["argv"])
    return got["argv"], keep, listen


def _keep_words(keep):
    return "nothing" if keep is None else json.dumps(keep, sort_keys=True)[:400]


def check_kept(request):
    """Step 4b: the request's ``keep`` against what this script reads of the unit's own
    command line, naming both when they differ, and each kept app's file read, so one that is
    not there refuses before anything is written. ``[{"path", "sha256"}]`` for the kept files
    the drop-in loads: the outcome records what Ryu loaded that Mercury does not manage."""
    argv, mine, _listen = read_unit(RYU_UNIT)
    if argv[0] != RYU_MANAGER:
        raise Refused("{}'s own ExecStart runs {}, and this script was installed for {}: "
                      "install it again with the host step, so nothing was done".format(
                          RYU_UNIT, argv[0], RYU_MANAGER))
    theirs = request.get("keep")
    if mine != theirs:
        raise Refused("the request carries {} of {}'s own command line, and this script reads "
                      "{} there: what the plan kept is not what the unit has, so nothing was "
                      "written".format(_keep_words(theirs), RYU_UNIT, _keep_words(mine)))
    out = []
    for app in kept_apps(request):
        if not app.endswith(".py"):
            continue
        try:
            with open(app, "rb") as fh:
                data = fh.read()
        except (IOError, OSError) as exc:
            raise Refused("the kept app {} cannot be read ({}): Ryu would not start with it, "
                          "so nothing was written".format(app, exc.strerror))
        out.append({"path": app, "sha256": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()})
    return out


def unit_read(argv):
    """The host step's read (the module's docstring): for the one unit *argv* names, print
    ``manager=`` its ryu-manager, ``rest=`` where Ryu's REST answers on the host itself
    (`rest_url`), ``app=`` each kept app's file and ``kept=`` what a deploy carries, and
    return 0; or print ``REFUSED: `` and why, and return 1. It reads `systemctl cat` and
    changes nothing."""
    try:
        if len(argv) != 1 or not UNIT_NAME.match(argv[0]):
            raise Refused("the unit's read takes one unit's name, <name>.service")
        command, keep, _listen = read_unit(argv[0])
    except Refused as exc:
        print("REFUSED: {}".format(exc))
        return 1
    keep = keep or {}
    print("manager={}".format(command[0]))
    print("rest={}".format(rest_url(keep.get("rest") or {})))
    for app in keep.get("apps") or []:
        if app.endswith(".py"):
            print("app={}".format(app))
    print("kept={}".format(json.dumps(keep, sort_keys=True)))
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3: the folders, and their content hash
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def blob_id(data):
    """Git's id for a blob of *data* (SHA-1 over its header and bytes), as hex."""
    return hashlib.sha1(b"blob " + str(len(data)).encode("ascii") + b"\0" + data).hexdigest()


def folder_entries(folder, account=None):
    """[(relative path bytes, git mode bytes, blob id bytes)] for every file under *folder*,
    refusing a link, anything not a file or directory, and (with *account*) an entry another
    owns or that group or others may write."""
    entries = []

    def unreadable(exc):
        raise Refused("{} in {} cannot be read ({})".format(
            os.path.relpath(exc.filename or folder, folder), folder, exc.strerror))

    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(folder, onerror=unreadable, followlinks=False):
        for name in sorted(dirs) + sorted(files):
            full = os.path.join(root, name)
            rel = os.path.relpath(full, folder).replace(os.sep, "/")
            st = os.lstat(full)
            if stat.S_ISLNK(st.st_mode):
                raise Refused("{} in {} is a symbolic link: a staged folder holds only files"
                              .format(rel, folder))
            if not (stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode) or stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode)):
                raise Refused("{} in {} is not a file or a directory".format(rel, folder))
            if account is not None:
                if st.st_uid != account.pw_uid:
                    raise Refused("{} in {} is owned by {}, not {}".format(
                        rel, folder, owner_words(st), DEPLOY_USER))
                if st.st_mode & (stat.S_IWGRP | stat.S_IWOTH):
                    raise Refused("{} in {} is {}: writable by group or others".format(
                        rel, folder, mode_words(st)))
            if stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
                with open(full, "rb") as fh:
                    data = fh.read()
                mode = b"100755" if st.st_mode & stat.S_IXUSR else b"100644"
                entries.append((rel.encode("utf-8", "surrogateescape"), mode,
                                blob_id(data).encode("ascii")))
    return entries


def folder_hash(folder, account=None):
    """The content hash of *folder* as it is on disk: Mercury's content hash
    (modules/jobs/lifecycle.content_hash) recomputed from the files' bytes."""
    entries = folder_entries(folder, account)
    if not entries:
        raise Refused("{} holds no file".format(folder))
    digest = hashlib.sha256(HASH_FRAMING)
    for rel, mode, obj in sorted(entries):
        digest.update(len(rel).to_bytes(8, "big") + rel + mode + b" "
                      + len(obj).to_bytes(1, "big") + obj)
    return digest.hexdigest()


def check_folders(request, account):
    root = os.path.realpath(APPS_ROOT)
    out = []
    for i, app in enumerate(request["apps"]):
        folder = os.path.join(root, app["name"], app["version"])
        where = "apps[{}]'s folder {}".format(i, folder)
        if os.path.realpath(folder) != folder:
            raise Refused("{} is not a real directory under {}: its realpath is elsewhere"
                          .format(where, root))
        try:
            st = os.lstat(folder)
        except OSError as exc:
            raise Refused("{} cannot be read ({})".format(where, exc.strerror))
        if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode):
            raise Refused("{} is not a directory".format(where))
        if st.st_uid != account.pw_uid:
            raise Refused("{} is owned by {}, not {}".format(where, owner_words(st),
                                                             DEPLOY_USER))
        entry = os.path.join(folder, app["name"] + ".py")
        if not os.path.isfile(entry) or os.path.islink(entry):
            raise Refused("{} holds no file {}.py".format(where, app["name"]))
        got = folder_hash(folder, account)
        if got != app["sha256"]:
            raise Refused("{}'s recomputed hash {} is not the request's {}: the folder changed "
                          "after it was staged".format(where, got, app["sha256"]))
        check_config(i, app, root, account)
        out.append(entry)
    return out


def sdk_folder(apps_root, sha256):
    """Where the app SDK of content hash *sha256* is staged: APPS_ROOT/.sdk/<sha256>."""
    return os.path.join(apps_root, SDK_DIR, sha256)


def check_sdk(request, account):
    """Step 3c (C2852, option A): the SDK folder the request names, its recomputed content hash
    the request's, holding mercury_app/__init__.py, nothing in it a link, another's or writable
    by group or others; None when the request names no SDK."""
    sdk = request.get("sdk")
    if sdk is None:
        return None
    root = os.path.realpath(APPS_ROOT)
    folder = sdk_folder(root, sdk["sha256"])
    where = "the app SDK's folder {}".format(folder)
    if os.path.realpath(folder) != folder:
        raise Refused("{} is not a real directory under {}: its realpath is elsewhere"
                      .format(where, root))
    try:
        st = os.lstat(folder)
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Refused("{} cannot be read ({})".format(where, exc.strerror))
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode):
        raise Refused("{} is not a directory".format(where))
    if st.st_uid != account.pw_uid:
        raise Refused("{} is owned by {}, not {}".format(where, owner_words(st), DEPLOY_USER))
    entry = os.path.join(folder, SDK_ENTRY)
    if not os.path.isfile(entry) or os.path.islink(entry):
        raise Refused("{} holds no file {}".format(where, SDK_ENTRY))
    got = folder_hash(folder, account)
    if got != sdk["sha256"]:
        raise Refused("{}'s recomputed hash {} is not the request's {}: the folder changed "
                      "after it was staged".format(where, got, sdk["sha256"]))
    return folder


def config_path(apps_root, name, version):
    """Where an app's start-time config is staged (decision K9): beside its version's folder,
    APPS_ROOT/<name>/<version>.config.json, so the folder's hash stays the reviewed code's."""
    return os.path.join(apps_root, name, version + CONFIG_SUFFIX)


def check_config(i, app, root, account):
    """Step 3b: the config file the request names (its sha256), or no config file at all."""
    path = config_path(root, app["name"], app["version"])
    where = "apps[{}]'s config {}".format(i, path)
    want = app.get("config_sha256")
    if want is None:
        if os.path.lexists(path):
            raise Refused("{} is there and the request names no config for it: the app would "
                          "read a config nobody confirmed".format(where))
        return
    if os.path.realpath(os.path.dirname(path)) != os.path.dirname(path):
        raise Refused("{} is not under a real directory: its folder's realpath is elsewhere"
                      .format(where))
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK)
    except OSError as exc:
        if exc.errno == errno.ELOOP:
            raise Refused("{} is a symbolic link, not a regular file".format(where))
        raise Refused("{} cannot be read ({})".format(where, exc.strerror))
    try:
        st = os.fstat(fd)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
            raise Refused("{} is not a regular file".format(where))
        if st.st_uid != account.pw_uid:
            raise Refused("{} is owned by {}, not {}".format(where, owner_words(st),
                                                             DEPLOY_USER))
        if st.st_mode & (stat.S_IWGRP | stat.S_IWOTH):
            raise Refused("{} is {}: writable by group or others".format(where,
                                                                          mode_words(st)))
        if st.st_nlink != 1:
            raise Refused("{} has {} links, not 1".format(where, st.st_nlink))
        if st.st_size > MAX_BYTES:
            raise Refused("{} is {} bytes, more than {}".format(where, st.st_size, MAX_BYTES))
        data = os.read(fd, MAX_BYTES + 1)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    got = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()
    if got != want:
        raise Refused("{}'s sha256 {} is not the request's {}: the config changed after it "
                      "was staged".format(where, got, want))
    try:
        doc = json.loads(data.decode("utf-8"))
    except (UnicodeDecodeError, ValueError):
        raise Refused("{} is not JSON in UTF-8".format(where))
    if not isinstance(doc, dict):
        raise Refused("{} is not a JSON object".format(where))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5 to 9: the drop-in, the restart, the outcome
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def request_sha256(request):
    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"))
                          .encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def render_dropin(request, ryu_manager, ryu_user, apps_root):
    """The one drop-in's text for *request* (Mercury's preview renders it the same way:
    modules/apps/channel.render_dropin, held equal by a test)."""
    files = [os.path.join(apps_root, a["name"], a["version"], a["name"] + ".py")
             for a in request["apps"]]
    # What the unit's own command line had that is not Mercury's to manage (step 4b): REST's
    # bind as the unit names it (never one it did not have), its other flags, and the apps it
    # loads that no app of the request replaces. A request with no keep renders as it always
    # did, byte for byte.
    keep = request.get("keep") or {}
    rest = keep.get("rest") or {}
    bind = ((["--wsapi-host", rest["host"]] if "host" in rest else [])
            + (["--wsapi-port", str(rest["port"])] if "port" in rest else []))
    command = ([ryu_manager] + list(FIXED_FLAGS)
               + ["--ofp-listen-host", request["listen"]["host"],
                  "--ofp-tcp-listen-port", str(request["listen"]["port"])]
               + bind + list(keep.get("flags") or []) + kept_apps(request)
               + files + list(BUILTIN_APPS))
    # The app SDK on the apps' import path (C2852, option A); a request naming none renders as
    # it always did, byte for byte.
    sdk = request.get("sdk")
    env = ("Environment=PYTHONPATH={}\n".format(sdk_folder(apps_root, sdk["sha256"]))
           if sdk else "")
    return ("# Rendered by mercury-ryu-apply for request {}. Mercury's next deploy replaces "
            "it; mercury.conf.prev is the one before.\n"
            "[Service]\nUser={}\n{}ExecStart=\nExecStart={}\n").format(
                request_sha256(request), ryu_user, env, " ".join(command))


def write_dropin(text):
    folder = os.path.join(DROPIN_ROOT, RYU_UNIT + ".d")
    if not os.path.isdir(folder):
        os.mkdir(folder, 0o755)
    path = os.path.join(folder, DROPIN_NAME)
    kept = False
    if os.path.lexists(path):
        if os.path.islink(path):
            raise Refused("{} is a symbolic link: nothing was written".format(path))
        with open(path, "rb") as fh:
            before = fh.read()
        _write_file(path + ".prev", before)
        kept = True
    _write_file(path, text.encode("utf-8"))
    return path, kept


def _write_file(path, data, mode=0o644):
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC | os.O_NOFOLLOW, mode)
    try:
        os.write(fd, data)
        os.fsync(fd)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    os.chmod(tmp, mode)
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def restart(before):
    """Steps 7 and 8: daemon-reload, restart, and success by identity within UP_BOUND_S.
    *before* is the MainPID read before the drop-in was written. A read of the unit that
    systemctl does not answer during the wait is a poll that read nothing, never a refusal:
    the drop-in is written and the unit restarted by then. The bound and ``up_after_s`` are
    counted on the monotonic clock from the moment `systemctl restart` returned (C2983): the
    wall clock steps when NTP corrects it, and a bound on it would then read years."""
    rc, _, err = systemctl("daemon-reload")
    if rc != 0:
        return {"ok": False, "step": "daemon-reload", "error": "systemctl daemon-reload "
                "answered {} ({})".format(rc, (err or "").strip()[:200]), "main_pid_before":
                before}
    rc, _, err = systemctl("restart", RYU_UNIT)
    started = time.monotonic()
    if rc != 0:
        return {"ok": False, "step": "restart", "error": "systemctl restart {} answered {} ({})"
                .format(RYU_UNIT, rc, (err or "").strip()[:200]), "main_pid_before": before}
    props, polls = {}, 0
    while True:
        polls += 1
        try:
            props = unit_properties("MainPID", "ActiveState", "User")
        except Refused:
            props = {}
        pid = props.get("MainPID", "")
        if props.get("ActiveState") == "active" and pid not in ("", "0", before) \
                and props.get("User") == RYU_USER:
            return {"ok": True, "step": "running", "main_pid_before": before,
                    "main_pid_after": pid, "active_state": "active", "user": RYU_USER,
                    "up_after_s": round(time.monotonic() - started, 1)}
        if time.monotonic() - started >= UP_BOUND_S:
            return {"ok": False, "step": "wait", "main_pid_before": before,
                    "main_pid_after": pid, "active_state": props.get("ActiveState", ""),
                    "user": props.get("User", ""),
                    "error": "{} was not active with a new MainPID and User={} within {} s of "
                             "`systemctl restart` returning ({}); `systemctl show` read {} "
                             "times: MainPID {} (before {}), ActiveState {}, User {}"
                             .format(RYU_UNIT, RYU_USER, UP_BOUND_S, UP_BOUND_SOURCE, polls,
                                     pid or "none", before or "none",
                                     props.get("ActiveState") or "none",
                                     repr(props.get("User", "")))}
        time.sleep(POLL_S)


def write_outcome(outcome):
    if not os.path.isdir(OUTCOME_DIR):
        os.makedirs(OUTCOME_DIR, 0o755)
    line = json.dumps(outcome, sort_keys=True)
    _write_file(os.path.join(OUTCOME_DIR, "outcome.json"), (line + "\n").encode("utf-8"))
    fd = os.open(os.path.join(OUTCOME_DIR, "history.jsonl"),
                 os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_APPEND | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o644)
    try:
        os.write(fd, (line + "\n").encode("utf-8"))
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def unrendered():
    return [n for n, v in (("RYU_UNIT", RYU_UNIT), ("RYU_MANAGER", RYU_MANAGER)) if "@" in v]


def apply(argv):
    if argv:
        raise Refused("{} takes no arguments, and was given {}".format(
            os.path.basename(sys.argv[0]), len(argv)))
    missing = unrendered()
    if missing:
        raise Refused("this copy was never rendered for its host ({} still a placeholder): "
                      "install it with the host step".format(", ".join(missing)))
    if REQUIRE_ROOT and os.geteuid() != 0:
        raise Refused("it runs as root (through its one sudoers line), not as uid {}".format(
            os.geteuid()))
    try:
        account = pwd.getpwnam(DEPLOY_USER)
    except KeyError:
        raise Refused("the deploy account {} does not exist".format(DEPLOY_USER))
    user = unit_properties("User").get("User", "")
    try:
        root_st = os.stat(APPS_ROOT)
    except OSError as exc:
        if exc.errno == errno.ENOENT:
            raise Refused("no request: {} does not exist".format(APPS_ROOT))
        raise Refused("{} cannot be read ({})".format(APPS_ROOT, exc.strerror))
    why = unsafe_refusal(user, root_st, account)
    if why:
        raise Refused(why)
    request = parse_request(read_request(account))
    if request.get("kind") == PUT_BACK:
        return put_back(request, user)
    files = check_folders(request, account)
    sdk = check_sdk(request, account)
    kept_files = check_kept(request)
    text = render_dropin(request, RYU_MANAGER, RYU_USER, os.path.realpath(APPS_ROOT))
    before = unit_properties("MainPID").get("MainPID", "")
    path, kept = write_dropin(text)
    result = restart_after_write(before)
    result.update({"request_sha256": request_sha256(request), "apps": request["apps"],
                   "listen": request["listen"], "files": files, "dropin": path,
                   "dropin_sha256": hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest(),
                   "prev_kept": kept, "user_before": user})
    if sdk is not None:
        result["sdk"] = sdk
    if "keep" in request:
        result["keep"] = request["keep"]
        result["kept_files"] = kept_files
    return result


def restart_after_write(before):
    """`restart`, with any exception past the drop-in's write an outcome of step after-write,
    never one that reads as nothing having changed (Mercury rolls back what landed)."""
    try:
        return restart(before)
    except Exception as exc:                            # noqa: BLE001 (the step says it)
        return {"ok": False, "step": "after-write", "main_pid_before": before,
                "error": "the drop-in was written, then {}: {}".format(type(exc).__name__,
                                                                       exc)}


def before_sha256(text):
    """The hash a put-back is bound to: of a drop-in's text with its leading and trailing blank
    lines dropped, which is how `systemctl cat` shows it and Mercury's plan reads it
    (modules/apps/channel.dropin_before)."""
    return hashlib.sha256((text.strip("\n") + "\n").encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def last_user(text):
    """The value of the last `User=` line of a drop-in's text (systemd takes the last), or
    None when it sets none."""
    found = None
    for line in text.splitlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if line.startswith("User="):
            found = line[len("User="):].strip()
    return found


def put_back(request, user):
    """Steps P1 to P3 (decision K3): mercury.conf.prev back as mercury.conf, then the restart
    judged by identity, as an apply's is."""
    folder = os.path.join(DROPIN_ROOT, RYU_UNIT + ".d")
    path = os.path.join(folder, DROPIN_NAME)
    prev = path + PREV_SUFFIX
    try:
        fd = os.open(prev, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK)
    except OSError as exc:
        if exc.errno == errno.ENOENT:
            raise Refused("there is no drop-in before to put back: {} does not exist".format(
                prev))
        if exc.errno == errno.ELOOP:
            raise Refused("{} is a symbolic link: nothing was written".format(prev))
        raise Refused("{} cannot be read ({})".format(prev, exc.strerror))
    try:
        st = os.fstat(fd)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
            raise Refused("{} is not a regular file".format(prev))
        if st.st_uid != os.geteuid():
            raise Refused("{} is owned by {}, not the account this script runs as (uid {}), "
                          "which wrote it".format(prev, owner_words(st), os.geteuid()))
        if st.st_mode & (stat.S_IWGRP | stat.S_IWOTH):
            raise Refused("{} is {}: writable by group or others".format(prev, mode_words(st)))
        if st.st_size > MAX_BYTES:
            raise Refused("{} is {} bytes, more than {}".format(prev, st.st_size, MAX_BYTES))
        data = os.read(fd, MAX_BYTES + 1)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    try:
        text = data.decode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeDecodeError:
        raise Refused("{} is not UTF-8".format(prev))
    got = before_sha256(text)
    if got != request["before_sha256"]:
        raise Refused("{} hashes {}, not the request's before_sha256 {}: it is not the drop-in "
                      "the plan read before the deploy, so nothing was written".format(
                          prev, got, request["before_sha256"]))
    set_user = last_user(text)
    if set_user != RYU_USER:
        raise Refused("{}'s last User= line is {}, not User={}: putting it back would not run "
                      "the unit as {}, so nothing was written".format(
                          prev, "absent" if set_user is None else repr(set_user), RYU_USER,
                          RYU_USER))
    if os.path.islink(path):
        raise Refused("{} is a symbolic link: nothing was written".format(path))
    replaced = None
    if os.path.lexists(path):
        with open(path, "rb") as fh:
            replaced = hashlib.sha256(fh.read()).hexdigest()
    before = unit_properties("MainPID").get("MainPID", "")
    _write_file(path, data)
    result = restart_after_write(before)
    result.update({"kind": PUT_BACK, "before_sha256": got, "dropin": path,
                   "dropin_sha256": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(),
                   "replaced_sha256": replaced, "user_before": user})
    return result


def main(argv):
    lock_fd, held = None, False
    started = iso()
    try:
        if not os.path.isdir(OUTCOME_DIR):
            os.makedirs(OUTCOME_DIR, 0o755)
        lock_fd = os.open(os.path.join(OUTCOME_DIR, "lock"),
                          os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lock_fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError:
            raise Refused("another apply holds {}".format(os.path.join(OUTCOME_DIR, "lock")))
        held = True
        outcome = apply(argv)
    except Refused as exc:
        outcome = {"ok": False, "refused": str(exc)}
    except Exception as exc:                            # noqa: BLE001 (written, then exit 1)
        outcome = {"ok": False, "error": "{}: {}".format(type(exc).__name__, exc)}
    outcome.update({"started": started, "finished": iso(), "unit": RYU_UNIT})
    try:
        if held:
            # Only the apply holding the lock writes the outcome: another's stays as written.
            write_outcome(outcome)
        else:
            outcome["outcome_not_written"] = "this run did not hold the lock"
    except OSError as exc:
        outcome["outcome_not_written"] = exc.strerror
    finally:
        if lock_fd is not None:
            os.close(lock_fd)
    print(json.dumps(outcome, sort_keys=True))
    return 0 if outcome.get("ok") else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
